\subsection{VTR Recovery}
\label{sec:vtr_recovery}

Vision Token Re-encoder (VTR) addresses the catastrophic cliff through learned re-encoding rather than hard deletion. A lightweight cross-attention module ($\sim$22M parameters, ${\sim}$5\% of SmolVLA) uses $M$ learned queries to attend over all 128 source tokens. VTR recovers SmolVLA from 0.0\% to over 60\% SR at 75\% compression ($M{=}32$: 60.1 $\pm$ 1.3\%, 3 seeds), where all hard pruning methods fail. The M-curve is flat: $M{=}16$ (87.5\% compression) matches $M{=}128$ (passthrough) within 1.1\,pp, confirming that learned re-encoding, not the compression ratio, is the operative factor. A parameter-matched MLP adapter achieves comparable performance (63.4 $\pm$ 2.6\%, $p = 0.15$), indicating the gain stems from re-encoding itself. Cross-suite evaluation confirms generalization: Spatial 53.2\% and Goal 56.4\%, both recovered from 0.0\%. Full results in Table~\ref{tab:vtr_results} (Appendix~\ref{app:vtr_full}).

